$ plumber config --help
exit: 0
--- stdout
Commands for viewing and managing Plumber configuration files.

Usage:
  plumber config [command]

Available Commands:
  diff        Display the difference between current config and defaults
  generate    Write the default .plumber.yaml template (commented)
  init        Interactive wizard for a tailored minimal .plumber.yaml
  migrate     Upgrade .plumber.yaml to the current schema (v2.0, per-provider, current control names)
  resolve     Print the fully resolved effective configuration
  slim        Rewrite a full .plumber.yaml as a minimal overlay
  validate    Validate a configuration file
  view        Display the effective configuration

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for config

Global Flags:
  -v, --verbose   Enable debug logging on stderr (level=debug); replaces the progress bar

Use "plumber config [command] --help" for more information about a command.

--- stderr

